{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "MAT",
  "chapter": 26,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it came to pass, when Jesus had finished all these sayings, he said to his disciples,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ye know that after two days is the passover, and the Son of man is betrayed to be crucified.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then assembled the chief priests, and the scribes, and the elders of the people, in the palace of the high priest, who was called Caiaphas,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And consulted that they might take Jesus by subtilty, and kill ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But they said, Not on the feast -",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": " day",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", lest there be an uproar among the people.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now when Jesus was in Bethany, in the house of Simon the leper,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There came to him a woman having an alabaster-box of very precious ointment, and poured it on his head as he sat ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "at table",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But when his disciples saw ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", they had indignation, saying, To what purpose ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " this waste?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For this ointment might have been sold for much, and given to the poor.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When Jesus understood ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", he said to them, Why trouble ye the woman? for she hath wrought a good work upon me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For ye have the poor always with you; but me ye have not always.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For in that she hath poured this ointment on my body, she did ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for my burial.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Verily I say to you, Wherever this gospel shall be preached in the whole world, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shall also this, which this woman hath done, be told for a memorial of her.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then one of the twelve, called Judas Iscariot, went to the chief priests,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And said, What will ye give me, and I will deliver him to you? And they covenanted with him for thirty pieces of silver.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And from that time he sought opportunity to betray him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now the first ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "day",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of the ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "feast of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " unleavened bread, the disciples came to Jesus, saying to him, Where wilt thou that we prepare for thee to eat the passover?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said, Go into the city to such a man, and say to him, The Master saith, My time is at hand; I will keep the passover at thy house with my disciples.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the disciples did as Jesus had appointed them; and they made ready the passover.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now when the evening was come, he sat down with the twelve.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And as they were eating, he said, Verily I say to you, that one of you will betray me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they were exceeding sorrowful, and began every one of them to say to him, Lord, is it I?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he answered and said, He that dippeth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hand with me in the dish, the same will betray me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The Son of man goeth, as it is written concerning him: but woe to that man by whom the Son of man is betrayed! it had been good for that man, if he had not been born.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then Judas, who betrayed him, answered and said, Master, is it I? He said to him, Thou hast said.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And as they were eating, Jesus took bread, and blessed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and broke ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and gave ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to the disciples, and said, Take, eat; this is my body.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he took the cup, and gave thanks, and gave ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to them, saying, Drink ye all of it;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For this is my blood of the new testament, which is shed for many for the remission of sin.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But I say to you, I will not drink henceforth of this fruit of the vine, until that day when I drink it new with you in my Father's kingdom.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when they had sung a hymn, they went out to the mount of Olives.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then saith Jesus to them, All ye shall be offended because of me this night: for it is written, I will smite the shepherd, and the sheep of the flock shall be scattered abroad.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But after I am risen again, I will go before you into Galilee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Peter answered and said to him, Though all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shall be offended because of thee, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "yet",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " will I never be offended.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Jesus said to him, Verily I say to thee, that this night, before the cock shall crow, thou wilt deny me thrice.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Peter said to him, Though I should die with thee, yet will I not deny thee. Likewise also said all the disciples.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.36",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.36",
      "verse": 36,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then cometh Jesus with them to a place called Gethsemane, and saith to the disciples, Sit ye here, while I go yonder and pray.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.37",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.37",
      "verse": 37,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he took with him Peter, and the two sons of Zebedee, and began to be sorrowful and very heavy.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.38",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.38",
      "verse": 38,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then saith he to them, My soul is exceeding sorrowful, even to death: tarry ye here, and watch with me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.39",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.39",
      "verse": 39,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he went a little further, and fell on his face, and prayed, saying, O my Father, if it is possible, let this cup pass from me: nevertheless, not as I will, but as thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "wilt",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.40",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.40",
      "verse": 40,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he cometh to the disciples, and findeth them asleep, and saith to Peter, What, could ye not watch with me one hour?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.41",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.41",
      "verse": 41,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Watch and pray, that ye enter not into temptation: the spirit indeed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " willing, but the flesh ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " weak.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.42",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.42",
      "verse": 42,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He went away again the second time, and prayed, saying, O my Father, if this cup may not pass away from me, except I drink it, thy will be done.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.43",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.43",
      "verse": 43,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he came and found them asleep again: for their eyes were heavy.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.44",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.44",
      "verse": 44,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he left them, and went away again, and prayed the third time, saying the same words.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.45",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.45",
      "verse": 45,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then he cometh to his disciples, and saith to them, Sleep on now, and take ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "your",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " rest: behold, the hour is at hand, and the Son of man is betrayed into the hands of sinners.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.46",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.46",
      "verse": 46,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Rise, let us be going: behold, he is at hand that doth betray me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.47",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.47",
      "verse": 47,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And while he was yet speaking, lo, Judas, one of the twelve, came, and with him a great multitude with swords and staffs, from the chief priests and elders of the people.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.48",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.48",
      "verse": 48,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now he that betrayed him, gave them a sign, saying, Whomsoever I shall kiss, that same is he; hold him fast.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.49",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.49",
      "verse": 49,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And forthwith he came to Jesus, and said, Hail Master; and kissed him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.50",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.50",
      "verse": 50,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Jesus said to him, Friend, Why art thou come? Then they came, and laid hands on Jesus, and took him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.51",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.51",
      "verse": 51,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And behold, one of them, who were with Jesus, stretched out ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hand, and drew his sword, and struck a servant of the high priest, and smote off his ear.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.52",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.52",
      "verse": 52,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then said Jesus to him, Put up again thy sword into its place: for all they that take the sword, shall perish by the sword.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.53",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.53",
      "verse": 53,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thinkest thou that I cannot now pray to my Father, and he will presently give me more than twelve legions of angels?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.54",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.54",
      "verse": 54,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But how then shall the scriptures be fulfilled, that thus it must be?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.55",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.55",
      "verse": 55,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In that same hour said Jesus to the multitudes, Are ye come out as against a thief with swords and staffs to take me? I sat daily with you teaching in the temple, and ye laid no hold on me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.56",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.56",
      "verse": 56,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But all this was done, that the scriptures of the prophets might be fulfilled. Then all the disciples forsook him, and fled.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.57",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.57",
      "verse": 57,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they that had laid hold on Jesus, led ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " away to Caiaphas the high priest, where the scribes and the elders were assembled.",
          "kind": "text"
