      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.58",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.58",
      "verse": 58,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But Peter followed him at a distance, to the high priest's palace, and went in, and sat with the servants to see the end.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.59",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.59",
      "verse": 59,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now the chief priests and elders, and all the council, sought false testimony against Jesus, to put him to death;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.60",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.60",
      "verse": 60,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But found none: and, though many false witnesses came, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "yet",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " found they none. At the last came two false witnesses,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.61",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.61",
      "verse": 61,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And said, This ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " said, I am able to destroy the temple of God, and to build it in three days.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.62",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.62",
      "verse": 62,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the high priest arose, and said to him, Answerest thou nothing, what ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is it which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " these testify against thee?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.63",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.63",
      "verse": 63,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But Jesus held his peace. And the high priest answered and said to him, I adjure thee by the living God, that thou tell us whether thou art the Christ the Son of God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.64",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.64",
      "verse": 64,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Jesus saith to him, Thou hast said: nevertheless I say to you, Hereafter shall ye see the Son of man sitting on the right hand of power, and coming in the clouds of heaven.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.65",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.65",
      "verse": 65,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then the high priest rent his clothes, saying, He hath spoken blasphemy; what further need have we of witnesses? behold, now ye have heard his blasphemy.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.66",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.66",
      "verse": 66,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What think ye? They answered and said, He is guilty of death.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.67",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.67",
      "verse": 67,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then they spit in his face, and buffetted him; and others smote ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with the palms of their hands,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.68",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.68",
      "verse": 68,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Saying, Prophesy to us, thou Christ, Who is he that smote thee?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MAT.26.69",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MAT.26.69",
      "verse": 69,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now Peter sat without in the palace: and a damsel came to him, saying, Thou also wast with Jesus of Galilee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
